>> title: Refried Beans, Instant Pot
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: beans, pinto, mexican, side, instant pot, pressure cooker, no soak
>> counters: Instant Pot
>> aka: instant pot refried beans, pressure cooker pinto beans, instant pot pinto beans, no soak pinto beans, frijoles refritos, refried pintos
>> servings: 8
>> dish: refried-beans
>> kit: Instant Pot
>> pairs-with: corn-tortillas
>> time: 1 hr 40 min
>> step.1: cook the pintos from dry, no soak — 40 min at high pressure
>> step.2: wait out the natural release 20 min, drain but keep the liquid
>> step.3: fry the onion in lard 6 min
>> step.4: mash the beans in
>> step.5: fry down 10 min until it holds a line

Put @dried pinto beans{1%lb}(450 g; dry, not soaked) into the #Instant Pot{} with @water{6%cups}(1.4 L), @white onion{1/2%large}(halved), @garlic{4%cloves} and @bay leaf{1}, lock the lid and ~pressure cook{40%min} at high pressure. Forty minutes is the long end of the published range for pintos from dry and it is the right end for this dish: refried beans get mashed, so the beans have to be past tender and into completely soft, and a pinto that is merely cooked makes a grainy mash you cannot rescue.

Let @&(~1)pot{} ~natural release{20%min} until the pin drops, then drain the beans and keep the cooking liquid — that is what the mash is loosened with, and pouring it away is how refried beans end up pasty. Pull the onion halves and the bay leaf.

Fry @yellow onion{1%small}(finely chopped) in @lard{1/3%cup}(70 g; or bacon fat) in the emptied inner pot on the highest Sauté setting ~fry{6%min}, until it is soft and the fat smells of it.

Add @&(~2)beans{} to @&(~1)onion{} with a cup of their cooking liquid and mash with a #potato masher{}, straight in the pot.

Fry @&(~1)beans{} on Sauté, stirring, until thick enough to hold a line, ~fry{10%min}, with @kosher salt{2 1/2%tsp} and @ground cumin{1/2%tsp}. This leg is the same as it ever was and it is not walk-away time: the pot's element is narrow and beans catch on it, so stand there and keep the spoon moving. Salt goes in here rather than in with the dry beans, where it would slow the skins down.
